pseudo-Boolean proof version 2.0
* Regression test (wrong verdict): the version 2.0 `pre_order` spelling of the
* `fresh_right` defect. Both proof versions feed the same
* `OrderFreshRightVariablesRule` into the same `TransitivityContext`, and the
* legacy parser also admits an empty list, so the version 2.0 form was
* exploitable in exactly the same way -- see
* incorrect/version3/def_order_transitivity_fresh_right_empty for the full
* story. The relation orders x1 < x2 < x3 < x1 and the formula is satisfied by
* `x1 = 1, x2 = 0, x3 = 0`, yet this used to verify as
* `s VERIFIED UNSATISFIABLE`.
f 4
pre_order cyc
    vars
        left u1 u2 u3
        right v1 v2 v3
        aux
    end
    def
        1 ~u1 1 v1 1 v2 >= 1 ;
        1 ~u2 1 v2 1 v3 >= 1 ;
        1 ~u3 1 v3 1 v1 >= 1 ;
    end
    transitivity
        vars
            fresh_right
        end
        proof
            proofgoal #1
                u >= 1 ;
            end -1
            proofgoal #2
                u >= 1 ;
            end -1
            proofgoal #3
                u >= 1 ;
            end -1
        end
    end
end
load_order cyc x1 x2 x3
dom >= 1 ; x1 -> x2 x2 -> x3 x3 -> x1 ; begin
    proofgoal #4
        u 1 ~x1 >= 1 ;
        u 1 ~x2 >= 1 ;
        u 1 ~x3 >= 1 ;
        u >= 1 ;
    end -1
end
output NONE
conclusion UNSAT
end pseudo-Boolean proof
